Reduce per-frame Image allocation for the spinner approach ring.

Same getScaledCopy() pattern as the circle approach ring. This block is
already brace-enclosed upstream, so no brace change is needed.

setAlpha now applies to the shared GameImage instance rather than a copy.
That is safe here because SPINNER_APPROACHCIRCLE is drawn only at this call
site and alpha is reassigned every frame immediately before the draw.

--- a/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/objects/Spinner.java
+++ b/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/objects/Spinner.java
@@ -226,9 +226,11 @@
 		GameImage.SPINNER_CIRCLE.getImage().setAlpha(alpha);
 		GameImage.SPINNER_CIRCLE.getImage().setRotation(drawRotation * 360f);
 		GameImage.SPINNER_CIRCLE.getImage().drawCentered(width / 2, height / 2);
 		if (!GameMod.HIDDEN.isActive()) {
 			float approachScale = 1 - Utils.clamp(((float) timeDiff / (hitObject.getTime() - hitObject.getEndTime())), 0f, 1f);
-			Image approachCircleScaled = GameImage.SPINNER_APPROACHCIRCLE.getImage().getScaledCopy(approachScale);
-			approachCircleScaled.setAlpha(alpha);
-			approachCircleScaled.drawCentered(width / 2, height / 2);
+			Image approachCircle = GameImage.SPINNER_APPROACHCIRCLE.getImage();
+			float acWidth = approachCircle.getWidth() * approachScale;
+			float acHeight = approachCircle.getHeight() * approachScale;
+			approachCircle.setAlpha(alpha);
+			approachCircle.draw(width / 2f - acWidth / 2f, height / 2f - acHeight / 2f, acWidth, acHeight);
 		}
